WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.520
They were the stupid years, what they were
doing was incredible,

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.880
NAFTA, one of the world's worst trade deals
ever, I know a couple of others

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.830
we've been involved in them too.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:12.800
By erecting tariffs and threatening to tear
up free trade agreements,

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.400
President Donald Trump has done more to advance
one of the left's long standing policy goals

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.029
than any other modern President.

00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:21.880
And he also sounds a lot like some of the
Democratic candidates

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.550
that are running to unseat him in the next
election.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:28.279
Bernie Sanders sill brags about how he opposed
the North American Free Trade Agreement

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.080
when it was ratified by Congress in 1994.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.920
In 2011, the Vermont Senator even went after
the Smithsonian Institution

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.520
for selling Chinese made toys.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:43.980
We should not be selling statues of the founding
fathers of this country

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.120
and have them made in China.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.399
From the World Trade Organization protests
in Seattle in 1999 to the 2016 campaign trail,

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.100
The left has traditionally opposed free trade
on the grounds that it hurts American workers.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:01.960
I hope in fact, all across the board, we begin
to focus on rebuilding our manufacturing sector

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.580
so that we create millions of jobs in products
made in the United States.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.460
But it's Donald Trump who has made at least
some of those dreams come true.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:14.000
We're asking Bernie Sanders voters to join
our movement.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.740
This creates a conundrum:

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:20.760
the Democrats running for office in 2020 can't
say that they like what Trump is doing

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:24.600
but they're also not really willing to criticize
his trade war.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.180
Your approach to trade with China is very
similar to the President's.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.000
No it is not.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.260
He's talking about how we're getting ripped
of left and right on trade.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:37.020
And I think you know I can take that paragraph
and just use it in my speeches

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.020
since what I'm saying it's one of my big things.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:43.980
US trade policy has delivered one punch in
the gut after another.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:48.620
Trump and anti-trade Democrats fail to grasp
that nations don't really trade with one another at all.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.620
Individuals and corporations do,

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.040
and sometimes those individuals and corporations

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.660
want to buy or sell something to someone in another country.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.799
And trade is the source of our wealth,

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:02.729
since 1950, international trade boosted Americans'
per household income

00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:04.480
by about 18 thousand dollars.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.960
And the gains flowed dis-proportionally to
lower income households.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:14.300
If they can save a nickel by moving a job
to Mexico, they'll do it in a heartbeat.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.820
Elizabeth is absolutely right,

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.530
for anybody here that thinks that corporate
America

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.500
gives one damn about the average American
worker, you're mistaken.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.860
But American manufacturing jobs peaked at
about 20 million in 1979.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.880
That's 15 years before NAFTA.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.849
Until bottoming out at 11.4 million in 2011.

00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:38.680
The reason for that decline isn't shifting
jobs overseas, it's automation.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.160
Manufacturing output has doubled since the
mid 1980s.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:48.140
America makes more stuff than ever, our factories
just don't require as many workers as they once did.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.180
Even supposedly centrist candidates like Senator
Kamala Harris

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.180
have shifted into protectionist mode.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:55.400
In an interview with Jake Tapper in May,

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.660
Harris said she wouldn't have voted for NAFTA
if she'd been in the Senate when it passed.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.739
I believe that we have got to have policy

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:07.349
that better protects American workers and
American industries.

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:09.980
Harris did criticize Trump's use of tariffs,

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.790
calling the President's habit of conducting
trade policy,

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:16.939
economic policy, foreign policy by tweet 'irresponsible.'

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.760
But that really drives home my point.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.400
Democrats seem happy to criticize Trump's
haphazard handling of the trade war.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:28.940
But many of the 2020 candidates are at least
tacitly endorsing the same protectionist views.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.720
Even Joe Biden, once a pro trade Democrat,

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:35.660
is now backing away from his record for fear
of upsetting the progressive left.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:40.310
I would not rejoin the TTP as it was initially
put forward.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:41.709
The Democrats are essentially arguing

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:45.540
that all we need is a more competent protectionist
in the White House.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.780
I think Trump gets it wrong in terms of implementation.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.299
But there's no way to correctly implement
a policy

00:03:52.299 --> 00:03:55.819
that stops individuals from freely exchanging
goods and services

00:03:55.819 --> 00:03:57.990
just because they live in different countries.

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:00.769
Thanks to President Donald Trump, Bernie Sanders'
vision

00:04:00.769 --> 00:04:05.340
of restricting our ability to peacefully trade
with one another has become policy.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.220
And that's a catastrophe for all Americans.

